#. Key:	Lobby_Host_Settings_ConnectionServicesTooltip
#. SourceLocation:	Localization/Data/LobbyUI.csv
#: Localization/Data/LobbyUI.csv
msgctxt "LobbyUI,Lobby_Host_Settings_ConnectionServicesTooltip"
msgid "The Connection Service handles two things: registering invite codes for dedicated servers and providing server information to clients (such as IP address, port, and routing points).\r\n\r\n<T_BOLD>In simple terms, all players in a co-op session need access to at least one shared Connection Service.</> If one player doesn’t have access to the same service as the others, they won’t be able to connect together.\r\n\r\nIt’s recommended to use a Connection Service that’s geographically close to you. Keep in mind this service only handles the initial handshake between your game client and the dedicated server, so it does not affect your in-game ping.\r\n\r\nIf all Connection Services appear unavailable, the only way to connect with your friends is by using Direct IP connection."
msgstr "The Connection Service handles two things: registering invite codes for dedicated servers and providing server information to clients (such as IP address, port, and routing points).\r\n\r\n<T_BOLD>In simple terms, all players in a co-op session need access to at least one shared Connection Service.</> If one player doesn’t have access to the same service as the others, they won’t be able to connect together.\r\n\r\nIt’s recommended to use a Connection Service that’s geographically close to you. Keep in mind this service only handles the initial handshake between your game client and the dedicated server, so it does not affect your in-game ping.\r\n\r\nIf all Connection Services appear unavailable, the only way to connect with your friends is by using Direct IP connection."

